= Grouping-frame numerator equivalence certificate

This is an exact, bounded factor-preserving equivalence certificate for the three original numerator-digest rows in crates/feynkit-generator/tests/generation_oracle/frames.rs. It establishes equality of the historical and current producer values, including every original grouped member, under the original frames and tensor interfaces. The expectation literals remain unchanged. A new independent Astra review is required before any targeted native-schema digest recertification.

== Frozen producers and request matrix

The historical source is 8d49e6ecf0d8fb1169e7433f2c0b41048aa92e60, with locked Symbolica c78cffc20f318df1fce50539a587cbe8ffc717c0. Its unmodified oracle binary passes all three original assertions without record mode. The current source is the fixed parent 59b57cead76e576fa9f23e3996f5614de939fe35, with locked Symbolica 1a1829b1f3d0a88b53b44085b3b9f34ef77945b3. Its hash-verified oracle binary reproduces the three numerator-digest failures; every other census field agrees. The test body differs only in import formatting and current failure capture. These are FeynKit-port expectations, not an assumption that older API-line digests are the native baseline.

All three requests use Classes::Auto, Naming::prefix("D"), a QED model with u, d, s and their antiparticles massless, and the corresponding mass symbols set to zero in their propagator numerator and denominator. The amplitude is e- e+ to a a at one loop without self loops. Its first row uses UpToSign with default grouping options; its second uses exact-particle Identical grouping with differentiate_particle_masses_only: false. The cross section is a a to e- e+ with two forward loops, one blob, zero spectators, no self loops, two-pass left/right symmetrization and the same exact-particle option. The full transformed effective model is retained independently for each producer and case under target/frame-certificate/model-hooks-{historical,current}/; the auxiliary frame-model.json agrees byte for byte. Each producer kernel recomputed its BLAKE3 ModelDefinition fingerprint from its own captured full model. All 1,572 pair-stage and 512 final graph model owner fields contain exactly that 32-byte fingerprint. The effective model has 118 parameters and 19 propagators; massless u/d/s edits, light propagator numerators and denominators, and the d/s denominator equality are checked from the actual effective model receipts.

Both routes enumerate and physically prepare the assignments; build once to obtain each diagram's named loop edges (captured in live first-build receipts); build again with those named bases and dot(0,4,0) + dot(1,6,1); re-prepare the comparison and representative frames; transport the requested prefactor and default projector through signed vertex, edge and half-edge maps; separately map the selected final internal loop edges; compare and group; then finalize the representative with cuts and source factors. The last confirmed shared physical boundary is complete source, comparison and representative graph incidence, rule and particle records, cut records, signed maps, exact loop signatures, factors and typed ports. The first different representation boundary is the graph constructor presentation tags and the explicit logical-interface serialization. No earlier input or physical graph mismatch was found.

