== Factorization and limits

The comparison reads frozen JSON and live owner metadata, binds only the audited presentation constructors, checks exact local and already-factorized aggregate strings, and proves the finite two-term prefactor identity and source ratios. It performs no whole-graph numerator expansion, Dirac trace or preparation, distribution of original mass-plus-slash factors, arbitrary coefficient normalization, interface omission or inference from numerical points. The graph's existing aggregate export calls fragment_numerator and SymbolicTensor::multiply_many. NumeratorInterface::export may then re-admit that aggregate to decide whether an interface needs serialization. This prerequisite was audited: admission's DotNormalizer::nested_vectors, tensor-power lowering and normalize_products do not distribute an original sum under graph multiplication or call Dirac algebra; named_product_expression assembles factors with Atom::mul_many and only compact rank-one dot contractions. The proof adds no algebra pass to that existing export path.

This certificate concerns exactly the three frozen rows and their members. It establishes neither a general grouping theorem nor a new physics, performance or distribution result. It does not assert that incompatible historical and current private tensor proof/cache histories are identical. The observed digest change is a native-schema representation boundary; only targeted digest recertification is proposed, after a new independent Astra review and later combined-tree validation. No expectation, production algorithm, lock, NixCI setting, push or upload was changed here.
